# The post-reload coherence case, run by the driver AFTER prober_signal_wait
# has confirmed a new worker is answering and the faulted request has finished
# erroring out. It proves the reloaded worker came back HEALTHY: a fresh,
# unfaulted request against the same memcached backend serves a correct 200,
# leaks no descriptor, and logs nothing new on the error path in the window
# around THIS request (the read-timeout from the faulted request necessarily
# logged an [error] earlier in the run; that is asserted and expected by the
# driver itself, not by this file -- see driver.sh's no_error_log discussion).
#
# The pid oracle is STRICT (no pid_may_change): by the time this runs, a
# single post-reload worker is serving, so both of this case's probe snapshots
# see the SAME worker and "same worker pid" is the correct, stronger assertion
# -- same reasoning as every sibling reload-*/post-reload.rule.

# SPLIT BY DESCRIPTOR KIND, not `delta fds == 0`. This scenario has exactly the
# profile that produces an intermittent NEGATIVE fd delta: it reloads a worker
# that is holding an upstream connection, and the old worker's socket is reaped
# asynchronously afterwards. A close landing inside the probe window drops the
# aggregate count by one, and `delta fds == 0` then reds on a descriptor
# CLOSING -- the opposite of the leak it exists to catch. Two sibling scenarios
# (backend-idle-close-reload, reload-worker-shutdown-timeout) were flaky for
# many sessions before that was understood; this one is written with the fix
# rather than waiting to earn it on CI.
#
# Only the socket bucket can legitimately fall here, so only it is relaxed, and
# only downwards -- an INCREASE still reds, which is the shape a leak takes.
# `delta` is `after - before`, so this rules out an UNOFFSET net increase; a
# leak exactly coinciding with the close nets to zero and passes, the same
# blind spot `delta fds == 0` has.

name    the reloaded worker serves a clean request after the mid-transfer fault
from    127.0.0.1
send    GET /mc?key=clean HTTP/1.1\r\n
send    Host: prober\r\nConnection: close\r\n\r\n
expect  status=200
delta   fds_by_kind.socket <= 0
delta   fds_by_kind.file == 0
delta   fds_by_kind.anon == 0
delta   fds_by_kind.other == 0
